<div class="glass-card glass-red glass-boss"><h2 id="wiki_warden_boss_fight"><label class="g-toggle"><input type="checkbox" class="g-cb"><span class="g-title">Warden Boss Fight<span class="g-tag">👹 BOSS</span></span><span class="g-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></label></h2>

<p id="guide-step-map-travel-to-nexus-core-and-stand-in-one-of-the-circles-to-start-the-enco">Travel to Nexus Core and stand in one of the circles to start the encounter. At the start of the fight, the Warden will take the form of a Scorpion-man. The Warden will move extremely fast, with the goal of pushing you out of the arena. The use of Void Claw (or Void Talon) is recommended. <ShowOnMap target="nexus-core" /></p>
<p><strong>Phase 1</strong> - The Warden is accompanied by a Dread Skull (weak to Dead Wire), destroying the Dread Skull will stun the Warden revealing a critical point at the end of its tail. Repeat the process until a third of the health is gone and the Warden becomes immune. While it is immune, Shadow Soul (weak to Light Mend) will appear around the map, destroy them all to start Phase 2.</p>
<p><strong>Phase 2</strong> - In addition to the Dread Skulls, the Warden will spawn floating circles that will stun and deal damages. Moreover, Warden's Stingers (weak to Cryofreeze) will appear around the arena. It is important to destroy as many stingers otherwise they can create a wipe attack. Continue until only a third of its health remains.</p>
<p><strong>Intermediate Phase</strong> - The Warden will send you to a close room where the objective will be to either survive a specific amount of time, or to eliminate a HVT. Once the objective is complete, you will be teleported back into the arena.</p>
<p><strong>Phase 3</strong> - Alongside the Warden's Stingers, circles, Dread Skulls, Shadow Souls will appear around the arena providing armor to the Warden and need to be destroyed. Repeat the same process until there is no more health.</p>
<p><strong>Phase 4</strong> - A surprise fourth phase will start. The Warden will have a third of health remaining and even more Shadow Souls providing armor. Additionally, several Dread Skulls need to be destroyed before the Warden can be stunned. Repeat the same process until the fight is finally done.</p></div>
<hr>
<h1 id="wiki_side_quests_and_easter_eggs">Side Quests and Easter Eggs</h1>


<div class="glass-card glass-violet"><h2 id="wiki_.22all_we_are.22_secret_song"><label class="g-toggle"><input type="checkbox" class="g-cb"><span class="g-title">"All We Are" Secret Song<span class="g-tag">🎵 Song</span></span><span class="g-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></label></h2>

<p id="guide-step-song-headphones" data-guide-step>Find three Mr Peeks headphones around the map: <ShowOnMap target="song-headphones" label="Show the three song headphone locations on map" /></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p id="guide-step-map-on-top-of-a-pillar-in-nyxara-main-chamber-requires-wall-jumping-to-rea">On top of a pillar in Nyxara Main Chamber, requires wall-jumping to reach.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p id="guide-step-map-at-a-window-in-ruinas-insula">At a window in Ruinas Insula.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Around a skull hidden between a rock and a low wall in Arena Insula.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MjpeDV0uVp4" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">"All We Are" by Kevin Sherwood and Elena Siegman</a></p></div>
<div class="glass-card glass-violet"><h2 id="wiki_masks"><label class="g-toggle"><input type="checkbox" class="g-cb" checked><span class="g-title">Masks<span class="g-tag">🎭 Masks</span></span><span class="g-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></label></h2>

<p>There are four masks available in Rex Infernus, all the masks can be used within the same game and each mask can be removed and placed on a specific pedestal to easily swap between them all.</p>
<h3 class="" id="wiki_horned_skull_mask_.28stone_cold_strongold_x_ring_of_fire.29">Horned Skull Mask (Stone Cold Strongold x Ring of Fire)</h3>
<ol>
<li id="guide-step-map-remain-inside-her-house-for-at-least-9-rounds">Remain inside Her House for at least 9 rounds. <ShowOnMap target="her-house" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-melee-the-painting-on-the-right-side-of-the-chimney-to-collect-the-hor">Melee the painting on the right side of the chimney to collect the <strong>Horned Skull Mask</strong>.

<ul>
<li><em>Note: Meleeing the painting after 5-6 rounds will reward with 600 Essence or some Ammo while after 7-8 rounds it will be either a free Perk can or a Rare Aether Tool.</em></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p>The Horned Skull Mask offers a damage and armor boost while standing still, with a circle that will damage any enemy entering it. <em>Note: There is a cooldown of 1 minute between each use.&nbsp;</em>The mask can be placed on the pedestal inside Veytharion Sanctuary.</p>
<h3 class="" id="wiki_cowboy_hat_mask_.28spider_immunity.29">Cowboy Hat Mask (Spider Immunity)</h3>
<ol>
<li>Ride a Web Mother next to the Pack-a-Punch machine and kill around 50 enemies. <em>Note: Riding the Web Mother is time-limited and may require several tries.</em></li>
<li>Once enough enemies have been killed, the Web Mother will jump into the Pack-a-Punch dying instantly and dropping the <strong>Cowboy Hat Mask</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p>The Cowboy Hat Mask offers some immunity against Deathspinners and Web Mothers. The mask can be placed on the pedestal inside Nyxara Inner Sanctum.</p>
<h3 class="" id="wiki_astronaut_helmet_mask_.28longer.2Dlasting_void_claw.29">Astronaut Helmet Mask (Longer-lasting Void Claw)</h3>
<ol>
<li id="guide-step-locations-her-house" data-guide-step>Collect six parts of Mr Peeks:
 <ShowOnMap target="locations-her-house" label="Show astronaut helmet mask (longer-lasting void claw) locations on map" />
<ul>
<li id="guide-step-map-the-head-is-on-a-shelf-in-her-house-next-to-quick-revive">The head is on a shelf in Her House next to Quick Revive.</li>
<li>A part is against a rock pillar just outside of Caltheris' Passage on the right side; requires the Void Claw.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-a-part-is-located-on-the-other-side-of-the-cliff-opposite-of-the-myste">A part is located on the other side of the cliff opposite of the Mystery Box location in Ruinas Insula; requires the Void Claw.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-a-part-is-located-floating-over-an-edge-below-the-main-ground-and-a-pl">A part is located floating over an edge below the main ground and a platform in Aranea Insula; requires the Void Claw.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-a-part-is-located-on-top-of-a-rock-pillar-above-juggernog-in-front-of-">A part is located on top of a rock pillar above Juggernog in front of the higher platform in Spira Insula; requires the Void Claw.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-a-part-is-located-outside-of-nexus-forge-in-between-veytharion-s-and-d">A part is located outside of Nexus Forge, in-between Veytharion's and Dravakar's temples; requires the Void Claw.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Make sure all the doors around the map are open.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-travel-to-caltheris-main-chamber-and-look-for-mr-peeks-on-the-ledge-of">Travel to Caltheris Main Chamber and look for Mr Peeks on the ledge of the platform above the Mystery Box location. <ShowOnMap target="caltheris-main-chamber" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-interact-with-mr-peeks-to-start-a-grappling-hook-parkour-course-cross-">Interact with Mr Peeks to start a Grappling Hook parkour course. Cross every Mr Peeks circle until it reaches the doorway of Nyxara Entrance. <ShowOnMap target="nyxara-entrance" /></li>
<li>Completing the parkour course in 50 seconds or less will drop the <strong>Astronaut Helmet</strong>, alongside other loot such as a Raw Aetherium Crystal.
<ul>
<li><em>Note: Complete the parkour course will reward with loot such as Essence, Salvaga and a Mystery Perk while completing it under a minute will aware a Ray Gun.</em></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p>The Astronaut Helmet offers an increased 30 seconds of use for the Void Claw and Void Talon. The mask can be placed on the pedestal in Caltheris Main Chamber on the platform above the Mystery Box location.</p>
<h3 class="" id="wiki_spiked_skull_mask_.28twins_ammo_effect.29">Spiked Skull Mask (Twins Ammo effect)</h3>
<ol>
<li id="guide-step-map-travel-to-the-forest-from-nyxara-inner-sanctum">Travel to the forest from Nyxara Inner Sanctum.
 <ShowOnMap target="nyxara-inner-sanctum" />
<ul>
<li><em>Note: This can be done once per round after the fruit has spawned.</em></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-interact-with-the-music-box-located-below-a-fallen-tree-trunk-and-leav">Interact with the music box located below a fallen tree trunk and leave the forest.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-return-to-the-forest-and-interact-with-a-blue-toy-box-located-between-">Return to the forest and interact with a blue toy box located between two trees.  <ShowOnMap target="nyxara-inner-sanctum" /></li>
<li>Three items will appear above the toy box, interacting with an item will trigger a mini-game by the Twins:
<ul>
<li><strong>Teddy Bear</strong>: Collect glowing plushies while being pursued by enemies who will move only when you're not looking before the time runs out.</li>
<li><strong>Mask</strong>: Quickly find the Twins before the time runs out. <em>Note: When the Twins are found, their energy will move towards the direction of their next spot.</em></li>
<li><strong>Rope</strong>: Do a skipping rope game, failing 3 times will end the mini-game.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Completing the Mask mini-game will reward with 1000 Essence; completing the Rope mini-game will reward with 600 Essence; and completing the Teddy Bear mini-game will reward with 600 Essence.
<ul>
<li><em>Note: Completing all the mini-games will reward with possible Aether Tool, Aetherium Crystal, Mystery Perk, and Wonder Weapon</em>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-return-to-the-forest-and-complete-all-three-mini-games-once-more-howev">Return to the forest and complete all three mini-games once more. However, the min-games will be harder to complete this time around

<ul>
<li><strong>Teddy Bear</strong>: Zombies are faster with less time to complete.</li>
<li><strong>Mask</strong>: Being stunned every time the Twins are found.</li>
<li><strong>Rope</strong>: Longer with more variation, failing 2 times will end the mini-game.</li>
</ul>
 <ShowOnMap target="nyxara-inner-sanctum" /></li>
<li>Completing the harder version of all the mini-games will reward with the same kind of loot as the normal version with the <strong>Spiked Skull Mask</strong> also becoming available.</li>
</ol>
<p>The Spiked Skull Mask offers a Twins ammo effect for your gun, the Twins will appear on the ground like a lightning strike kill all the zombies nearby. The mask can be placed on the pedestal inside Dravakar Sanctuary, on the left of the Armor wall-buy and doorway.</p></div>
<div class="glass-card glass-violet"><h2 id="wiki_mr._peeks.27_dance_off"><label class="g-toggle"><input type="checkbox" class="g-cb"><span class="g-title">Mr. Peeks' Dance Off<span class="g-tag">🕺 Dance Off</span></span><span class="g-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></label></h2>

<ol>
<li id="guide-step-map-with-the-void-claw-open-the-various-dig-spots-until-one-of-them-drops-">With the Void Claw, open the various Dig Spots until one of them drops a glowing cassette. <ShowOnMap target="dig-spots" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-travel-to-aranea-insula-and-find-the-cassette-player-interact-with-the">Travel to Aranea Insula and find the cassette player. Interact with the player to place the cassette. <ShowOnMap target="aranea-insula" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-if-done-correctly-you-will-be-teleported-to-her-house-to-complete-a-ry">If done correctly, you will be teleported to Her House to complete a rythm mini-game. Buttons will be shown on screen and needs to be pressed in the correct order before the time runs out. <ShowOnMap target="her-house" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-once-the-mini-game-is-finished-a-trophy-will-appear-in-nexus-forge-con">Once the mini-game is finished, a trophy will appear in Nexus Forge containing loot and Essence. <ShowOnMap target="nexus-forge" /></li>
</ol></div>
<div class="glass-card glass-gold"><h2 id="wiki_corrupted_weapons"><label class="g-toggle"><input type="checkbox" class="g-cb"><span class="g-title">Corrupted Weapons<span class="g-tag">☢️ Corrupted</span></span><span class="g-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></label></h2>

<h3 class="" id="wiki_corrupted_press_f">Corrupted Press F</h3>
<ol>
<li id="guide-step-map-purchase-the-m34-novaline-from-dravakar-sanctuary">Purchase the M34 Novaline from Dravakar Sanctuary. <ShowOnMap target="dravakar-sanctuary" /></li>
